Changes: the agents panel also draws the pantheon plugin's Codex jobs, read
from its session state (`pantheon.jobs`) when that plugin is installed: as
cards and swimlanes on the subagents' time axis, marked `codex`, `codex bg`
(running in the background) or `codex lost` (its process gone), with a live
clock while a job runs, and a `codex` legend entry. The default
`architectPattern` also matches `oracle`, so pantheon's oracle counts as the
architect. The hooks are unchanged and
still pass every event on as it came. The manifest's homepage and repository
point to this marketplace; the README installs from spider-claude-mods, loads
its images from the upstream repository and drops the upstream-only files
(CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, docs/media).
